Lake fetches the foundation and Mathlib at those commits and takes the cpap-np-hardness and cpap-minor-free
packages from this repository. The generated Challenge.lean specification reproduces verbatim the
definitions of hypermaps and their planarity from the NP-completeness foundation
(Complexity/Planarity.lean), the definitions of the cycle-path assignment problem from the
cpap-np-hardness library and the definition of K4 from the cpap-minor-free library, as their
documentation asks downstream developments to do, and imports three modules of Mathlib.

Outerplanar/RAM/Model.lean and Outerplanar/RAM/Spec.lean are copies of the corresponding files
of the cpap-approximation-hardness package of the same manuscript (same authors, Apache-2.0); see their
module documentation.
